1
00:01:55,098 --> 00:01:55,876
Where is Bu-nga?

2
00:01:56,327 --> 00:01:57,178
Why isn't she here?

3
00:01:57,578 --> 00:01:58,501
What did you do

4
00:01:58,930 --> 00:02:00,109
to make Bu-nga and Khem

5
00:02:00,269 --> 00:02:01,301
disappear...

6
00:02:01,636 --> 00:02:03,323
since the night Nora Jiam died.

7
00:02:03,621 --> 00:02:04,552
Nora Jiam is dead?

8
00:02:05,672 --> 00:02:07,178
I know you hate your daughter-in-law,

9
00:02:07,309 --> 00:02:08,981
but I never thought you’d be this ruthless.

10
00:02:11,730 --> 00:02:14,429
May she get exactly what she deserves.

11
00:02:15,374 --> 00:02:16,807
May she rot in hell

12
00:02:17,330 --> 00:02:19,090
and never find peace.

13
00:02:26,596 --> 00:02:28,312
Khem and Bu-nga are key witnesses.

14
00:02:28,872 --> 00:02:30,749
Until I find them,

15
00:02:30,952 --> 00:02:32,349
I won’t go back to the capital.

16
00:02:33,658 --> 00:02:35,200
Even if no one believes

17
00:02:35,352 --> 00:02:36,538
or sees you,

18
00:02:37,818 --> 00:02:39,200
the heavens saw

19
00:02:39,338 --> 00:02:40,450
what you did.

20
00:02:45,694 --> 00:02:47,207
How can I help you?

21
00:02:52,138 --> 00:02:52,720
Stop!

22
00:02:53,250 --> 00:02:53,840
Stop it!

23
00:02:54,349 --> 00:02:54,938
Let go of her!

24
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,087
Get out!

25
00:02:58,727 --> 00:02:59,861
Stay away from my child!

26
00:03:15,047 --> 00:03:16,545
Hear my curse.

27
00:03:17,185 --> 00:03:19,061
May you and your kin

28
00:03:19,389 --> 00:03:21,418
utterly perish

29
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:23,643
for all eternity

30
00:03:28,589 --> 00:03:31,556
Rest in peace, Bu-nga.

31
00:03:31,912 --> 00:03:32,865
Liar!

32
00:03:34,749 --> 00:03:35,992
Word is,

33
00:03:37,905 --> 00:03:39,432
Bu-nga took her revenge.

34
00:03:47,425 --> 00:03:50,749
Lukchan lost her mother.
She needs you.

35
00:03:51,272 --> 00:03:54,007
Take Lukchan back to the capital at once.

36
00:03:54,436 --> 00:03:55,512
What about you?

37
00:03:56,043 --> 00:03:57,607
I have something to take care of.

38
00:04:11,396 --> 00:04:13,752
Did Ploy and the child leave safely?

39
00:04:17,890 --> 00:04:19,752
We’re all each other now.

40
00:04:20,705 --> 00:04:21,520
From now on,

41
00:04:21,607 --> 00:04:23,069
I’ll look after you, Thep.

42
00:04:24,050 --> 00:04:25,905
After Duangkhae died,

43
00:04:26,843 --> 00:04:29,898
Lady Mok has been acting strange.

44
00:04:29,963 --> 00:04:30,785
Excuse me.

45
00:04:32,050 --> 00:04:36,676
The way she looked at Thep was different.

46
00:04:37,592 --> 00:04:39,880
It was pure lust.

47
00:04:41,287 --> 00:04:42,945
What did you want with him?

48
00:04:43,723 --> 00:04:45,192
You’ve been hounding him lately.

49
00:04:47,061 --> 00:04:47,570
Well...

50
00:04:47,927 --> 00:04:51,330
I just asked him to help Raj with school.

51
00:05:54,465 --> 00:05:55,454
Don't go in there.

52
00:05:55,629 --> 00:05:56,210
Khem!

53
00:05:58,530 --> 00:05:59,592
Where have you been?

54
00:06:00,996 --> 00:06:01,578
Khem!

55
00:06:02,981 --> 00:06:04,334
You can’t stay here.

56
00:06:05,047 --> 00:06:05,985
Leave the country with me.

57
00:06:08,472 --> 00:06:09,061
Please, Khem.

58
00:06:22,145 --> 00:06:23,047
You should go, Master.

59
00:06:23,469 --> 00:06:24,356
Get as far away as you can.

60
00:06:24,618 --> 00:06:25,905
I'm staying.

61
00:06:27,047 --> 00:06:27,570
Khem

62
00:06:30,414 --> 00:06:31,054
Please leave.

63
00:06:31,294 --> 00:06:31,898
Please.

64
00:06:33,134 --> 00:06:33,912
Go!

65
00:06:35,316 --> 00:06:35,963
What’s happening?

66
00:06:36,203 --> 00:06:36,850
Go!

67
00:06:38,981 --> 00:06:40,021
Whoa!

68
00:06:43,309 --> 00:06:44,283
Hurry, Master!

69
00:06:45,294 --> 00:06:45,847
Khem!

70
00:06:46,661 --> 00:06:47,323
What happened?

71
00:06:47,461 --> 00:06:48,181
Run!

72
00:06:48,349 --> 00:06:49,236
- Hurry!
- Khem!

73
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:23,098
Bu-nga!

74
00:07:24,690 --> 00:07:25,192
Ah!

75
00:07:28,858 --> 00:07:30,029
Don't sin any further.

76
00:07:30,370 --> 00:07:31,134
I'm begging you.

77
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:36,421
If I’d known you were doing evil,

78
00:07:37,170 --> 00:07:38,538
I never would have helped.

79
00:07:44,254 --> 00:07:44,945
Khem,

80
00:07:48,123 --> 00:07:48,894
help...

81
00:07:52,276 --> 00:07:53,003
me...

82
00:07:58,283 --> 00:07:59,745
with one last favor?

83
00:08:03,200 --> 00:08:03,694
Yes.

84
00:08:05,898 --> 00:08:06,960
Take my ashes...

85
00:08:07,745 --> 00:08:08,800
mine...

86
00:08:09,607 --> 00:08:10,087
and...

87
00:08:10,785 --> 00:08:11,432
my father's.

88
00:08:13,600 --> 00:08:14,800
Bury them...

89
00:08:17,010 --> 00:08:18,465
with the keris...

90
00:08:21,069 --> 00:08:22,545
under the house.

91
00:08:24,247 --> 00:08:25,738
Keep it a secret.

92
00:08:27,752 --> 00:08:29,200
Can you do that?

93
00:08:31,527 --> 00:08:32,967
And what they did to me...

94
00:08:34,261 --> 00:08:35,738
was that not a sin too?

95
00:08:38,370 --> 00:08:39,374
Especially you.

96
00:08:43,716 --> 00:08:45,090
You told me...

97
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:46,698
to just go die.

98
00:08:48,007 --> 00:08:48,705
Bu-nga,

99
00:08:49,345 --> 00:08:50,494
do you remember?

100
00:08:51,454 --> 00:08:52,581
You loved Thep.

101
00:08:56,836 --> 00:08:57,403
Love?

102
00:09:00,363 --> 00:09:01,738
I really love you.

103
00:09:10,749 --> 00:09:12,400
I no longer believe you.

104
00:09:19,425 --> 00:09:19,970
Ah!

105
00:09:39,905 --> 00:09:40,392
Master.

106
00:09:40,705 --> 00:09:41,512
Don't!

107
00:09:41,665 --> 00:09:42,232
Thep!

108
00:09:43,810 --> 00:09:44,989
Listen to me.

109
00:10:07,127 --> 00:10:07,760
Bu-nga

110
00:10:08,349 --> 00:10:09,294
Please let him go.

111
00:10:11,956 --> 00:10:12,712
Stay out of this!

112
00:10:22,843 --> 00:10:23,840
If you don't stop,

113
00:10:24,530 --> 00:10:26,203
I’ll dig up your bones and the keris.

114
00:10:33,680 --> 00:10:34,640
Let's go.

115
00:10:36,385 --> 00:10:37,003
Careful.

116
00:10:41,570 --> 00:10:42,101
Come on.

117
00:10:50,210 --> 00:10:51,170
Take it slow.

118
00:11:47,643 --> 00:11:48,618
Whatever we...

119
00:11:48,843 --> 00:11:49,934
owe each other,

120
00:11:52,203 --> 00:11:53,803
I’ll repay my debt...

121
00:11:54,167 --> 00:11:55,418
in the next life.

122
00:12:12,305 --> 00:12:13,018
Khem!

123
00:12:15,010 --> 00:12:15,636
Khem!

124
00:12:25,461 --> 00:12:27,265
This doesn't concern you.

125
00:12:27,483 --> 00:12:28,021
Khem!

126
00:12:39,032 --> 00:12:40,080
If my life...

127
00:12:41,025 --> 00:12:42,516
can repay you,

128
00:12:48,647 --> 00:12:49,592
then take it.

129
00:12:51,905 --> 00:12:52,901
Then die...

130
00:12:53,127 --> 00:12:54,240
for me.

131
00:13:44,734 --> 00:13:47,381
He asks you to spare him.

132
00:13:59,229 --> 00:14:01,236
Karma is real.

133
00:14:02,436 --> 00:14:04,807
Our lives have come to this

134
00:14:05,665 --> 00:14:07,163
all because of our karma.

135
00:14:08,610 --> 00:14:10,450
It's not up to us.

136
00:14:11,301 --> 00:14:12,160
Please,

137
00:14:13,280 --> 00:14:14,152
stop it.

138
00:14:40,618 --> 00:14:42,654
Ultimately, Khem died too.

139
00:14:43,738 --> 00:14:47,752
Thep spoke little of what occurred.

140
00:14:48,530 --> 00:14:50,989
Rumors of Bu-nga faded

141
00:14:51,716 --> 00:14:54,152
as the deaths finally stopped.

142
00:14:54,843 --> 00:14:58,196
They believed Monk Sawang vanquished

143
00:14:58,538 --> 00:15:00,349
the ghost while on pilgrimage.

144
00:15:02,632 --> 00:15:04,770
Thep entered the monkhood
for the rest of his days.

145
00:15:05,570 --> 00:15:08,087
He never lived with Ploy,

146
00:15:09,156 --> 00:15:11,629
but left Lukchan in her care.

147
00:15:12,370 --> 00:15:14,996
He followed the monk on his pilgrimage,

148
00:15:15,730 --> 00:15:18,029
and neither was seen again.

149
00:15:23,941 --> 00:15:24,669
Ploy

150
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:28,174
Ploy!

151
00:15:29,323 --> 00:15:30,072
Ploy!

152
00:15:32,356 --> 00:15:33,730
She's gone.

153
00:15:49,352 --> 00:15:50,029
Ploy

154
00:15:56,800 --> 00:15:57,534
Ploy!

155
00:15:58,203 --> 00:15:59,018
Ploy!

156
00:16:05,745 --> 00:16:07,607
Never leave Thep's side.

157
00:16:08,210 --> 00:16:08,836
Ploy!

158
00:16:14,130 --> 00:16:14,923
Ploy!

159
00:16:24,865 --> 00:16:26,043
We have to get out of here.

160
00:16:36,327 --> 00:16:37,047
Chanchao,

161
00:16:37,309 --> 00:16:38,254
come with me.

162
00:16:41,825 --> 00:16:42,734
This child

163
00:16:42,981 --> 00:16:44,356
was never your own.

164
00:16:50,712 --> 00:16:51,861
And this man

165
00:16:52,007 --> 00:16:53,345
was never yours to have.

166
00:16:57,650 --> 00:16:58,203
Ploy,

167
00:16:59,665 --> 00:17:00,203
let's go.

168
00:17:00,923 --> 00:17:02,720
We can’t just leave her!

169
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:04,029
I’m not going!

170
00:17:31,003 --> 00:17:31,789
Come here.

171
00:17:32,494 --> 00:17:33,309
Let's pray.

172
00:17:35,738 --> 00:17:37,869
May you have a long life,
beauty, happiness,

173
00:17:38,421 --> 00:17:39,076
and strength.

174
00:17:42,894 --> 00:17:44,996
From now on, I'll look after you.

175
00:17:58,043 --> 00:17:58,850
Let it go, Ploy.

176
00:17:59,541 --> 00:18:01,047
We need to find help.

177
00:18:11,920 --> 00:18:13,556
Chanchao, come with me.

178
00:18:14,036 --> 00:18:14,945
Please!

179
00:18:25,912 --> 00:18:29,789
[Chanting in Pali]

180
00:18:30,145 --> 00:18:38,829
[Chanting in Pali]

181
00:18:38,880 --> 00:18:39,774
Chanchao!

182
00:18:43,578 --> 00:18:44,429
Chanchao!

183
00:18:47,527 --> 00:18:48,283
Chanchao!

184
00:19:08,276 --> 00:19:10,749
You took my child from me again!

185
00:19:19,730 --> 00:19:20,523
Wait.

186
00:19:22,261 --> 00:19:24,029
Are we leaving Jomthap behind?

187
00:19:31,883 --> 00:19:32,334
Hey!

188
00:19:33,156 --> 00:19:34,029
- Jomthap!
- Jomthap!

189
00:19:36,196 --> 00:19:37,301
Where have you been?

190
00:19:44,901 --> 00:19:48,741
I see now the evil Lady Mok
brought upon this house.

191
00:19:49,323 --> 00:19:51,469
I’m ashamed to be her blood.

192
00:19:52,538 --> 00:19:54,821
Now I know why I returned

193
00:19:55,294 --> 00:19:57,534
to claim what was never mine.

194
00:19:58,792 --> 00:20:01,156
Please, keep us all safe.

195
00:20:01,680 --> 00:20:03,476
And I will make amends.

196
00:20:03,992 --> 00:20:05,396
I will bring justice

197
00:20:05,701 --> 00:20:07,265
to those who deserve it.

198
00:21:09,592 --> 00:21:10,640
I'm sorry

199
00:21:12,632 --> 00:21:14,283
for everything.

200
00:21:16,341 --> 00:21:17,367
Duangkhae.

201
00:22:13,490 --> 00:22:14,632
I think we're going the wrong way.

202
00:22:18,560 --> 00:22:21,265
I hope we aren't lost like our first day here.

203
00:22:25,650 --> 00:22:27,585
I should have known since that day.

204
00:22:28,443 --> 00:22:31,585
Something’s been off since we arrived.

205
00:22:34,880 --> 00:22:35,694
It's my fault.

206
00:22:36,690 --> 00:22:37,912
I insisted we stay here.

207
00:22:39,120 --> 00:22:39,941
I know

208
00:22:40,130 --> 00:22:40,763
the reason.

209
00:23:19,614 --> 00:23:20,203
Hey!

210
00:23:52,509 --> 00:23:53,272
Hey!

211
00:24:01,250 --> 00:24:03,178
Ah!

212
00:24:04,407 --> 00:24:05,810
You are all going to die!

213
00:24:16,472 --> 00:24:17,112
Bu-nga

214
00:24:17,847 --> 00:24:19,061
If you still think I'm Khem,

215
00:24:19,192 --> 00:24:19,985
then just listen.

216
00:24:22,814 --> 00:24:24,320
I have Luang Decha's diary.

217
00:24:25,520 --> 00:24:26,916
You can kill me once you’ve heard this.

218
00:24:55,920 --> 00:24:58,007
I learned your story from this book.

219
00:25:00,029 --> 00:25:00,887
Both before you died,

220
00:25:01,825 --> 00:25:03,207
and after.

221
00:25:05,883 --> 00:25:07,760
Luang Decha was locked in the basement.

222
00:25:10,116 --> 00:25:12,400
Because he recorded everything
that happened to our family

223
00:25:12,865 --> 00:25:13,738
in this diary.

224
00:25:37,105 --> 00:25:38,210
After you died,

225
00:25:41,134 --> 00:25:42,494
no one was ever happy again.

226
00:25:43,716 --> 00:25:45,120
Even Thep, who survived,

227
00:25:46,021 --> 00:25:47,054
never left for abroad.

228
00:25:47,992 --> 00:25:48,887
He didn't live with his child

229
00:25:49,330 --> 00:25:50,196
or Ploy.

230
00:25:51,047 --> 00:25:52,421
He was ordained as a monk for life.

231
00:26:02,756 --> 00:26:04,094
He followed Monk Sawang

232
00:26:04,603 --> 00:26:05,338
on a forest pilgrimage.

233
00:26:14,414 --> 00:26:16,058
And they were never seen again.

234
00:26:20,814 --> 00:26:22,363
I believe he ordained to save you

235
00:26:24,872 --> 00:26:26,305
and everyone else who died.

236
00:26:33,585 --> 00:26:34,560
But unfortunately,

237
00:26:35,709 --> 00:26:37,789
his time to pray for everyone

238
00:26:38,312 --> 00:26:39,250
was cut short.

239
00:26:43,978 --> 00:26:44,989
He contracted jungle fever

240
00:26:46,450 --> 00:26:48,094
and died on the trail.

241
00:27:01,963 --> 00:27:04,821
Only Sawang returned with the news.

242
00:27:17,301 --> 00:27:18,523
But when he arrived at the mansion,

243
00:27:19,549 --> 00:27:21,003
he only found Lady Mok.

244
00:27:21,672 --> 00:27:24,712
She claimed he’d lost his mind

245
00:27:26,087 --> 00:27:27,345
and simply vanished.

246
00:27:29,003 --> 00:27:30,618
But he never really left.

247
00:27:53,250 --> 00:27:53,905
Master!

248
00:28:23,570 --> 00:28:25,330
How dare you?

249
00:28:25,920 --> 00:28:27,367
I'm your master!

250
00:28:28,116 --> 00:28:28,901
Let me go!

251
00:28:29,345 --> 00:28:30,247
I said, let me go!

252
00:28:30,385 --> 00:28:31,112
Let go!

253
00:28:31,621 --> 00:28:33,861
I’m the one in charge now.

254
00:28:37,883 --> 00:28:38,560
Mok!

255
00:28:38,989 --> 00:28:40,247
You betrayed me.

256
00:28:44,007 --> 00:28:45,738
Look at yourself in the mirror.

257
00:28:47,112 --> 00:28:48,640
How old are you?

258
00:28:49,018 --> 00:28:50,763
You wanted a young wife.

259
00:28:50,901 --> 00:28:52,225
Who could put up with that?

260
00:28:52,676 --> 00:28:54,101
You said you loved me.

261
00:28:55,520 --> 00:28:57,367
I love your money.

262
00:28:58,087 --> 00:28:58,690
And...

263
00:28:59,156 --> 00:29:00,930
if Thep were still alive,

264
00:29:02,094 --> 00:29:05,534
I’d still be playing nice.

265
00:29:06,974 --> 00:29:08,152
But too bad...

266
00:29:08,945 --> 00:29:10,880
he died far too young.

267
00:29:14,116 --> 00:29:15,905
And without that Bu-nga,

268
00:29:16,880 --> 00:29:18,400
he and I...

269
00:29:19,178 --> 00:29:21,018
might have had a chance.

270
00:29:22,130 --> 00:29:23,490
What does he have to do with this?

271
00:29:24,581 --> 00:29:25,869
I loved him.

272
00:29:26,698 --> 00:29:28,581
I loved him from the start.

273
00:29:29,156 --> 00:29:31,440
But he never looked at me.

274
00:29:32,647 --> 00:29:35,665
Because of you.

275
00:29:38,509 --> 00:29:41,025
Then there were Bu-nga and Ploy too.

276
00:29:41,934 --> 00:29:44,269
Lady Mok locked him in the cellar.

277
00:29:45,760 --> 00:29:48,087
She confessed to burning the house down.

278
00:29:50,116 --> 00:29:53,120
Are you making chicken curry?

279
00:29:53,614 --> 00:29:54,196
Yes.

280
00:29:54,814 --> 00:29:56,050
Let me help

281
00:29:56,203 --> 00:29:57,287
so we can finish sooner.

282
00:29:58,160 --> 00:30:00,734
The Lady isn't fond of chicken breast.

283
00:30:00,996 --> 00:30:02,458
She says it's too dry.

284
00:30:04,880 --> 00:30:06,487
Lady Mok hated Duangkhae

285
00:30:06,618 --> 00:30:07,716
for being snobbish

286
00:30:08,618 --> 00:30:09,760
and looking down on her.

287
00:30:10,909 --> 00:30:12,218
She was also jealous of Bu-nga

288
00:30:12,821 --> 00:30:13,847
for getting Thep.

289
00:30:14,807 --> 00:30:16,727
She turned them against each other.

290
00:30:19,200 --> 00:30:20,865
Here's the chicken curry.

291
00:30:22,290 --> 00:30:23,832
I wanted you to try it.

292
00:30:34,974 --> 00:30:36,269
Did something bite you?

293
00:30:36,378 --> 00:30:37,149
I don't know.

294
00:30:37,563 --> 00:30:38,785
- Oh my god!
- I'm suddenly itching.

295
00:30:39,301 --> 00:30:40,610
You have a rash.

296
00:30:40,894 --> 00:30:41,454
You!

297
00:30:42,770 --> 00:30:43,600
Bu-nga!

298
00:30:43,803 --> 00:30:45,745
- Did you put eggs in this?
- No.

299
00:30:48,261 --> 00:30:48,967
Bu-nga,

300
00:30:49,330 --> 00:30:50,378
make sure you don't add eggs.

301
00:30:50,560 --> 00:30:51,367
She's allergic.

302
00:30:52,443 --> 00:30:53,578
Good thing Khem spoke up.

303
00:30:54,865 --> 00:30:55,781
I'm glad you told me.

304
00:30:57,454 --> 00:30:59,512
Don't forget, I'm Raj's own grandson,

305
00:30:59,970 --> 00:31:01,098
Lady Mok's son.

306
00:31:02,458 --> 00:31:04,901
Why would I blacken my own family's name?

307
00:31:18,603 --> 00:31:20,465
Lady Mok’s jewelry is missing.

308
00:31:21,200 --> 00:31:22,370
We've searched everywhere

309
00:31:22,458 --> 00:31:24,152
and still can't find them.

310
00:31:25,672 --> 00:31:26,480
Bu-nga!

311
00:31:26,785 --> 00:31:29,214
How dare you steal Lady Mok's bracelet?

312
00:31:29,898 --> 00:31:30,872
Did you find it?

313
00:31:31,330 --> 00:31:32,312
Right here.

314
00:31:32,734 --> 00:31:34,363
First, you tried to kill the Lady.

315
00:31:34,676 --> 00:31:36,400
Now you steal from Lady Mok.

316
00:31:36,625 --> 00:31:38,261
You’re nothing but a born thief.

317
00:31:39,061 --> 00:31:41,061
I really didn't do it.

318
00:31:41,512 --> 00:31:43,316
I believe Bu-nga is innocent.

319
00:31:44,123 --> 00:31:45,687
She’s being framed

320
00:31:45,898 --> 00:31:47,534
You dare suspect me?

321
00:31:48,050 --> 00:31:50,189
Because you think I’m a wicked woman.

322
00:31:50,356 --> 00:31:51,912
How dare you raise your voice?

323
00:31:53,200 --> 00:31:54,036
Lock her up.

324
00:31:54,443 --> 00:31:56,160
Don't let her see the light of day.

325
00:32:00,254 --> 00:32:02,501
Mok conspired with the head servant

326
00:32:03,069 --> 00:32:04,160
to brainwash Bu-nga.

327
00:32:11,410 --> 00:32:12,196
And turn her

328
00:32:12,370 --> 00:32:13,527
against Duangkhae

329
00:32:15,032 --> 00:32:15,956
and Ploy.

330
00:32:21,294 --> 00:32:21,905
Bu-nga

331
00:32:22,603 --> 00:32:23,338
Are you awake?

332
00:32:24,116 --> 00:32:24,945
I have a letter for you.

333
00:32:34,865 --> 00:32:36,145
And the worst part

334
00:32:36,705 --> 00:32:37,338
is that

335
00:32:39,410 --> 00:32:41,258
Mok sent a hitman for Bu-nga

336
00:32:42,327 --> 00:32:43,803
and framed Duangkhae.

337
00:32:50,865 --> 00:32:52,189
The killer never talked

338
00:32:53,520 --> 00:32:55,403
because she silenced him.

339
00:32:59,403 --> 00:33:00,720
Feed him.

340
00:33:01,432 --> 00:33:02,538
Then poison him.

341
00:33:03,934 --> 00:33:06,036
Dead men tell no tales.

342
00:33:08,741 --> 00:33:10,087
And this is for you.

343
00:33:12,749 --> 00:33:14,320
Get it done.

344
00:33:15,723 --> 00:33:16,538
Yes.

345
00:33:24,632 --> 00:33:27,781
Everyone believed Duangkhae was the killer.

346
00:33:43,156 --> 00:33:44,145
Darling.

347
00:33:48,850 --> 00:33:50,458
I'm scared of ghosts.

348
00:34:04,349 --> 00:34:05,890
Put these in the cellar.

349
00:34:13,105 --> 00:34:15,236
Mok got rid of all of
Duangkhae's belongings.

350
00:34:17,090 --> 00:34:19,069
She made it seem like
Duangkhae never lived there.

351
00:34:21,556 --> 00:34:24,225
Luang Decha never thought
she'd target him, too.

352
00:34:39,032 --> 00:34:40,443
Eat quickly, Master.

353
00:34:40,778 --> 00:34:41,949
I'll be back for the plates soon.

354
00:34:53,425 --> 00:34:54,901
A loyal servant...

355
00:34:56,087 --> 00:34:57,781
smuggled food and water to him.

356
00:34:59,010 --> 00:35:01,105
He asked for a journal.

357
00:35:16,800 --> 00:35:18,305
Please deliver this letter...

358
00:35:19,214 --> 00:35:20,465
to Ploy.

359
00:35:26,945 --> 00:35:28,160
I'm begging you.

360
00:36:03,730 --> 00:36:04,756
Where have you been?

361
00:36:15,527 --> 00:36:16,472
I asked you...

362
00:36:16,683 --> 00:36:18,269
where you were.

363
00:36:28,312 --> 00:36:28,909
Let go!

364
00:36:55,527 --> 00:36:56,640
Think you’re clever?

365
00:36:58,792 --> 00:37:01,767
Trying to write to Ploy?

366
00:37:07,163 --> 00:37:08,400
You have no right

367
00:37:09,636 --> 00:37:11,367
to lock me up here.

368
00:37:12,785 --> 00:37:15,549
I hold the power of life and death

369
00:37:16,007 --> 00:37:17,854
over this house.

370
00:37:18,996 --> 00:37:20,763
Including you.

371
00:37:24,472 --> 00:37:25,956
Then just kill me!

372
00:37:27,018 --> 00:37:28,698
As you wish.

373
00:37:29,854 --> 00:37:33,309
Let's see how long you last

374
00:37:34,000 --> 00:37:35,934
without food.

375
00:37:41,701 --> 00:37:43,578
I curse you.

376
00:37:45,396 --> 00:37:47,054
May you die a wretched death.

377
00:37:48,858 --> 00:37:50,741
Rot in hell

378
00:37:52,036 --> 00:37:53,541
for all eternity.

379
00:38:09,970 --> 00:38:12,145
He gathered his strength to write the journal,

380
00:38:13,425 --> 00:38:15,781
hoping the truth would one day be told.

381
00:38:17,934 --> 00:38:19,985
Even if he wasn't there to see it.

382
00:38:37,490 --> 00:38:38,516
My baby.

383
00:38:39,425 --> 00:38:40,254
My child.

384
00:38:44,283 --> 00:38:45,316
My baby.

385
00:38:49,883 --> 00:38:50,938
My sweet girl.

386
00:39:11,890 --> 00:39:12,909
My baby.

387
00:39:14,160 --> 00:39:14,916
My child.

388
00:39:22,887 --> 00:39:23,854
Mom?

389
00:39:27,912 --> 00:39:28,712
Chanchao!

390
00:39:48,916 --> 00:39:50,981
More concerning than her wounds

391
00:39:51,083 --> 00:39:52,261
is her blood.

392
00:39:52,727 --> 00:39:55,381
You both know about her condition, right?

393
00:39:58,290 --> 00:39:59,047
Yes.

394
00:39:59,352 --> 00:40:02,174
We don't have enough
Type B blood in our bank.

395
00:40:02,385 --> 00:40:04,254
We have to wait for
the Red Cross to send some.

396
00:40:04,676 --> 00:40:07,629
Only then can we assess her condition.

397
00:40:16,501 --> 00:40:17,614
I have Type B blood.

398
00:40:19,738 --> 00:40:20,872
I can donate.

399
00:40:24,378 --> 00:40:24,938
But...

400
00:40:25,185 --> 00:40:25,970
Excuse me.

401
00:40:26,072 --> 00:40:27,934
What are her underlying conditions?

402
00:40:29,280 --> 00:40:30,807
She has hemophilia.

403
00:40:30,894 --> 00:40:32,407
It's a bleeding disorder.

404
00:40:33,141 --> 00:40:34,232
I have it too.

405
00:40:34,720 --> 00:40:36,501
But isn't that a genetic disorder?

406
00:40:36,625 --> 00:40:38,916
- That means one of you...
- Neither of us is a carrier.

407
00:40:48,341 --> 00:40:49,934
Actually, the two of us...

408
00:40:50,240 --> 00:40:52,080
aren't her biological parents.

409
00:41:28,887 --> 00:41:31,709
I got her real mother's name
from the orphanage.

410
00:41:33,563 --> 00:41:34,909
Her name is Namkang.

411
00:41:41,214 --> 00:41:42,487
I still don't know your name.

412
00:41:43,636 --> 00:41:44,850
What for?

413
00:41:45,127 --> 00:41:46,465
You’ll forget it by tomorrow.

414
00:41:47,934 --> 00:41:48,516
Come on.

415
00:41:48,596 --> 00:41:49,360
Tell me.

416
00:41:51,570 --> 00:41:52,421
Nam.

417
00:41:53,221 --> 00:41:54,043
Nam.

418
00:41:55,127 --> 00:41:55,956
Nam and?

419
00:41:56,894 --> 00:41:57,701
Namtarn?

420
00:41:57,854 --> 00:41:58,647
Namwan?

421
00:41:58,763 --> 00:41:59,512
Nampun?

422
00:42:00,029 --> 00:42:01,396
Nam...

423
00:42:01,723 --> 00:42:02,836
Namkang.

424
00:42:04,261 --> 00:42:05,207
Namkang.

425
00:42:17,592 --> 00:42:18,123
Oh...

426
00:42:18,865 --> 00:42:20,036
Hey, Jomthap.

427
00:42:57,840 --> 00:42:59,614
If you had shown me some mercy,

428
00:43:03,018 --> 00:43:04,036
I wouldn't have...

429
00:43:04,414 --> 00:43:06,436
been turned against you.

430
00:43:08,560 --> 00:43:10,603
And things wouldn't have gotten this bad.

431
00:43:11,665 --> 00:43:12,683
The people I love

432
00:43:13,396 --> 00:43:16,160
wouldn't have to suffer from my curse.

433
00:43:25,854 --> 00:43:27,025
Think about it carefully.

434
00:43:28,661 --> 00:43:33,185
Was it really all their fault?

435
00:43:39,389 --> 00:43:40,574
You can see me?

436
00:43:42,036 --> 00:43:43,738
I have always seen you.

437
00:43:46,370 --> 00:43:49,258
We share the blood of Nora.

438
00:43:50,341 --> 00:43:52,123
We are kin.

439
00:44:46,523 --> 00:44:48,130
If only you had stayed mindful

440
00:44:48,749 --> 00:44:51,730
and let go of your malice.

441
00:44:53,061 --> 00:44:55,985
It wouldn’t have come to

442
00:44:56,152 --> 00:44:58,829
the point you offer

443
00:44:59,498 --> 00:45:01,469
a life for a curse.

444
00:45:01,992 --> 00:45:03,752
The deeper the hate,

445
00:45:03,898 --> 00:45:07,694
the stronger the curse.

446
00:45:09,258 --> 00:45:11,032
But you probably never thought

447
00:45:11,534 --> 00:45:13,476
that the consequences would return

448
00:45:14,080 --> 00:45:15,781
to the people you love

449
00:45:15,912 --> 00:45:17,701
the most in this lifetime.

450
00:45:29,512 --> 00:45:31,447
Why must I suffer...

451
00:45:33,163 --> 00:45:35,134
both in life and in death?

452
00:45:42,981 --> 00:45:46,247
Why didn't karma find Mok?
She started this.

453
00:45:48,021 --> 00:45:49,694
You weren't always with her.

454
00:45:50,421 --> 00:45:52,029
How could you know...

455
00:45:52,690 --> 00:45:54,392
she didn't face the consequences?

456
00:45:55,549 --> 00:45:56,196
Even...

457
00:45:56,385 --> 00:45:58,945
you were there,

458
00:45:59,658 --> 00:46:01,345
how do you know...

459
00:46:01,730 --> 00:46:03,629
she wasn't suffering?

460
00:46:09,614 --> 00:46:10,872
Where are you going?

461
00:46:11,432 --> 00:46:13,294
You gave me a pox!

462
00:46:13,810 --> 00:46:15,469
You're lucky I don't kill you.

463
00:46:16,276 --> 00:46:17,854
Stay here.

464
00:46:18,000 --> 00:46:19,207
Please don't go anywhere.

465
00:46:19,541 --> 00:46:21,498
And let the whole village gossip?

466
00:46:24,574 --> 00:46:25,280
You!

467
00:46:25,578 --> 00:46:26,938
What are you doing to me?

468
00:46:27,403 --> 00:46:28,349
Let me go!

469
00:46:30,138 --> 00:46:31,149
Let me go!

470
00:46:31,360 --> 00:46:32,298
Let me go!

471
00:46:32,385 --> 00:46:33,687
Keep your filth away from me!

472
00:46:42,552 --> 00:46:43,461
Does hell

473
00:46:43,912 --> 00:46:45,163
really exist?

474
00:46:46,007 --> 00:46:47,287
No one can say.

475
00:46:48,625 --> 00:46:50,887
But the hell in one’s mind is real.

476
00:46:51,490 --> 00:46:53,367
Those who commit bad deeds

477
00:46:54,021 --> 00:46:56,254
will see their karma return

478
00:46:56,600 --> 00:46:57,960
in the end.

479
00:46:58,669 --> 00:47:01,810
Our only task is to stop the cycle.

480
00:47:02,480 --> 00:47:03,629
That's all.

481
00:47:09,338 --> 00:47:10,930
I want it all to end.

482
00:47:12,720 --> 00:47:14,763
I’ll gladly burn in hell

483
00:47:19,461 --> 00:47:21,469
if it saves Lukchan and Khem

484
00:47:22,480 --> 00:47:25,120
from that family's fate.

485
00:47:26,509 --> 00:47:28,247
Let go of your hate...

486
00:47:28,443 --> 00:47:30,545
and truly forgive.

487
00:47:31,258 --> 00:47:34,792
Forgive those who wronged you.

488
00:47:35,214 --> 00:47:39,003
Then perhaps the curse will break.

489
00:48:20,756 --> 00:48:21,730
I have something to return.

490
00:48:22,865 --> 00:48:24,305
What Mok did

491
00:48:24,509 --> 00:48:25,490
was truly

492
00:48:25,614 --> 00:48:26,530
horrific.

493
00:48:27,243 --> 00:48:28,603
I have no respect for her,

494
00:48:28,814 --> 00:48:30,945
but I can’t hate my own blood.

495
00:48:32,109 --> 00:48:36,123
And I believe she’s already paid the price.

496
00:48:36,661 --> 00:48:38,378
Even if we didn’t see it.

497
00:48:42,683 --> 00:48:46,356
I’m starting to believe that
no meeting is a coincidence.

498
00:48:47,054 --> 00:48:48,523
And that I am here...

499
00:48:48,894 --> 00:48:50,218
for a reason.

500
00:50:55,789 --> 00:50:57,418
Chanchao had her Nora class today.

501
00:50:57,970 --> 00:50:59,701
I'll take her to get a passport tomorrow.

502
00:51:00,683 --> 00:51:03,585
Anyway, are you and your mom sure

503
00:51:04,167 --> 00:51:06,109
you can handle this little rascal?

504
00:51:07,825 --> 00:51:10,218
If she’s too much,
I’ll send her back away.

505
00:51:11,032 --> 00:51:11,549
Wait,

506
00:51:11,658 --> 00:51:12,749
what's that noise?

507
00:51:13,156 --> 00:51:14,450
It’s for the Tenth Lunar Month Festival.

508
00:51:14,960 --> 00:51:17,120
The villagers are on their way to make merit.

509
00:51:18,792 --> 00:51:22,509
Southerners believe
spirits visit their kin today.

510
00:51:22,690 --> 00:51:24,938
You’re a Southerner.
You should know that.

511
00:51:25,825 --> 00:51:26,349
Yes.

512
00:51:27,156 --> 00:51:29,338
I hope Bu-nga can visit her child.

513
00:51:29,956 --> 00:51:31,192
If she knows,

514
00:51:31,985 --> 00:51:33,650
she’d be so proud of Chanchao.
